From 4bdc307d6de288600b20421055722da26ac79310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ian <ian.laffey@mail.mcgill.ca>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 01:42:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] AP_NavEKF3: companion-supplied wind + ground bootstrap
 fixes

Three related changes bundled here because they all touch
NavEKF3_core::setLatLng and the new NavEKF3_core::setExternalWind:

  1. Add setExternalWind() so the companion can directly inject the
     EKF's wind state. Wires AP_AHRS::set_external_wind_estimate to
     call EKF3 as well as DCM, so the existing MAVLink command
     MAV_CMD_EXTERNAL_WIND_ESTIMATE (43004) reaches the EKF. Reject
     the call when onGround (stationary zero-vel fusion runs there
     and wind state has no role until takeoff).

  2. Remove the inFlight gate from bootstrap_allowed in setLatLng so
     the companion can bootstrap the EKF on the ground. Without this
     the EKF stays in AID_NONE until takeoff, AHRS.get_location
     returns false, and Plane::navigate() short-circuits before ever
     calling L1.update_waypoint (so AUTO mission never runs).

  3. Seed the velocity state to airspeed*(cos yaw, sin yaw) on the
     first bootstrap, gated on airspeed > 5 m/s. Without seeding the
     EKF can converge to the backward-velocity branch of the
     airspeed/sideslip fusion solution set (|v - wind| = TAS has two
     roots) and report ground velocity 180 deg from truth. Gating on
     airspeed > 5 m/s means a covered pitot on the ground doesn't
     bake a bogus velocity into the state; stationary zero-vel fusion
     pins it to 0 until takeoff.

  4. Also bypass the dead-reckon freshness gate when bootstrap_allowed
     is true. EKF init pins lastGpsPosPassTime_ms to imuSampleTime_ms,
     so without this the first ground bootstrap call would be rejected
     for the first ~deadReckonDeclare_ms (~4s) even though no GPS data
     is actually flowing.
